  "materialRecognition": {
    "verdict": "PASS",
    "material": "Aged lime plaster with matte green and red mineral pigment, worn lower red over dark substrate, and shallow ochre/gold plaster meander ornament. Exact historic composition remains uncertain.",
    "observations": "Canonical RGB and actual decoded Mid256x512 and High512x1024 depict recognisable physical plaster: irregular aggregate, coherent shallow trowelled surface, local chips/flakes and worn pigment over a dark support. Natural fine structure follows larger wear rather than a uniform noise overlay. The lower weathered red area remains legible painted material, not an arbitrary noisy procedural fill. High is visibly photographic at 1:1; Mid preserves that material character at its intended scale."
  },
  "formsColourAndScale": {
    "verdict": "PASS representative similarity",
    "observations": "Large grey-green upper field, narrow red bands, small ochre meander at the original vertical position and worn dark-red lower field retain their native proportions, colour relationships and character. The new curves and damaged surface edges are natural rather than enlargements of native pixel steps. No invented small bricks, objects, image-perimeter bevel, vignette frame or unrelated architectural form appears."
  },
